content="<think>\nAlright, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user's instructions. Let me go through each task step by step.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with '---' on the first line. That's straightforward. I'll make sure to include that.\n\nNext, each task has a specific name and description. I'll list them out to ensure I don't miss any.\n\nTask 1 is about creating directories for cadvisor with proper permissions. I'll use the file module with state=directory and set the owner and group appropriately.\n\nTask 2 requires downloading the cadvisor binary from a URL, including checksum verification. I'll use the get_url module and specify the checksum.\n\nTask 3 is to copy the binary from a local directory to the installation directory and notify a restart handler. I'll use the copy module and add a notify for the handler.\n\nTask 4 involves creating a symbolic link. I'll use the ln module with state=symlink.\n\nTask 5 is about creating a systemd service file from a template. I'll use the template module for this.\n\nTask 6 checks if the cadvisor service is active and registers the result. I'll use the shell module and register the output.\n\nTask 7 is a debug task to display the service_active variable. I'll use the debug module with var=service_active.\n\nTask 8 enables the cadvisor systemd service. I'll use the systemctl module with enable.\n\nTask 9 starts the service and ensures it's running. I'll use systemctl with start and enabled options.\n\nI need to ensure all tasks are correctly ordered and use the right modules. Also, the playbook should be valid YAML and conform to lint standards.\n\nI'll structure each task with the appropriate module and arguments. For the copy task, I'll make sure the remote_src is set to yes if needed. The notify will trigger the restart handler.\n\nFor the template task, I'll specify the destination path and any variables if necessary. The shell command in task 6 will check the service status and register it.\n\nThe debug task will simply output the variable to verify the status. The enable and start tasks will ensure the service is running at boot and now.\n\nI think that covers all the tasks. Now, I'll write the YAML playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: cadvisor | create directories\n  file:\n    path: /opt/cadvisor\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: cadvisor | download\n  get_url:\n    url: https://github.com/google/cadvisor/releases/download/v2.7.0/cAdvisor-linux-amd64.tar.gz\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor.tar.gz\n    checksum: sha256:abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef\n\n- name: cadvisor | propagate locally distributed cadvisor binary\n  copy:\n    src: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor.tar.gz\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/\n    remote_src: yes\n  notify: restart_cadvisor\n\n- name: cadvisor | symlink\n  ln:\n    src: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/cadvisor\n    state: symlink\n\n- name: cadvisor | server systemd service\n  template:\n    src: cadvisor.service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/cadvisor.service\n\n- name: test_task\n  shell: systemctl status cadvisor | grep 'active'\n  register: service_active\n\n- name: debug: var=service_active\n  debug:\n    var: service_active\n\n- name: cadvisor | enable server systemd\n  systemctl:\n    name: cadvisor\n    state: enabled\n\n- name: cadvisor | start server systemd\n  systemctl:\n    name: cadvisor\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:00:27.213266319Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12596121832, 'load_duration': 81451308, 'prompt_eval_count': 494, 'prompt_eval_duration': 103599328, 'eval_count': 806, 'eval_duration': 12410244791, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--9322dee1-cc0e-46df-921b-d008f4430257-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 494, 'output_tokens': 806, 'total_tokens': 1300}
