vice. Maybe the issue is elsewhere.\n\nWait, looking back, the third error is about line 37 having a syntax error. Line 37 is part of the "systemctl" task under "cadvisor | start server systemd." The task is:\n\n- name: cadvisor | start server systemd\n  systemctl:\n    name: cadvisor\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\nAh, here the "enabled" parameter is set to "yes," which is a string, but the error suggests it should be a boolean. So, I should change "yes" to true. But wait, the "enabled" parameter in Ansible\'s systemctl module expects a boolean. So, yes, changing "yes" to true would fix this.\n\nWait, but looking at the task description, Task 8 is to enable the service, and Task 9 is to start it. So, in Task 8, the "systemctl" call is for enabling, and in Task 9, it\'s for starting. However, in the faulty playbook, Task 8 has "state: enabled," which is correct, and Task 9 has "state: started" and "enabled: yes." That\'s incorrect because the "enabled" parameter in Task 9\'s "systemctl" call should not be set as "yes" but rather should be omitted or set to true if necessary. Wait, no, the "enabled" parameter is for whether the service should be enabled, so in Task 9, perhaps it\'s redundant because the service is already enabled in Task 8.\n\nBut the main issue is that in Task 9, the "enabled" parameter is set to "yes," which is a string, but the error expects it to be a boolean. So, I need to change "enabled: yes" to "enabled: true." However, looking at the Ansible documentation, the "enabled" parameter is a boolean, so it should be set to true or false.\n\nWait, but in Ansible, the "systemctl" module\'s "enabled" parameter is a boolean. So, "enabled: yes" is incorrect. It should be "enabled: true." Therefore, I need to correct that.\n\nAdditionally, the third error is about a syntax issue at line 37, which is part of the "systemctl" task in Task 9. So, the error is likely due to the "enabled: yes" being incorrect, as it\'s not a boolean.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I\'ll make the following changes:\n\n1. Split the long line in the "copy" task to adhere to the 80-character limit by formatting it with multiple lines.\n\n2. Correct the "enabled" parameter in the "systemctl" task under Task 9 from "yes" to "true."\n\nI\'ll go through each task to ensure that these changes are applied without altering any other parts of the playbook.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: cadvisor | create directories\n  file:\n    path: /opt/cadvisor\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: cadvisor | download\n  get_url:\n    url: https://github.com/google/cadvisor/releases/download/v2.7.0/cAdvisor-linux-amd64.tar.gz\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor.tar.gz\n    checksum: sha256:abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef\n\n- name: cadvisor | propagate locally distributed cadvisor binary\n  copy:\n    src: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor.tar.gz\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/\n    remote_src: yes\n  notify: restart_cadvisor\n\n- name: cadvisor | symlink\n  ln:\n    src: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/cadvisor\n    state: symlink\n\n- name: cadvisor | server systemd service\n  template:\n    src: cadvisor.service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/cadvisor.service\n\n- name: test_task\n  shell: systemctl status cadvisor | grep \'active\'\n  register: service_active\n\n- name: debug: var=service_active\n  debug:\n    var: service_active\n\n- name: cadvisor | enable server systemd\n  systemctl:\n    name: cadvisor\n    state: enabled\n\n- name: cadvisor | start server systemd\n  systemctl:\n    name: cadvisor\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:00:52.613893392Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 24982786185, 'load_duration': 89321884, 'prompt_eval_count': 950, 'prompt_eval_duration': 334442600, 'eval_count': 1418, 'eval_duration': 24557860481, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--12e