uring they match the user\'s instructions. Looks like all tasks are accounted for, and the playbook starts with \'---\' as required.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Wait for port to be available\n  wait_for_port:\n    port: "{{ some_port }}"\n    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout }}"\n\n- name: Prepare system\n  raw:\n    cmd: "{{ command_to_test_connection }}"\n  become: false\n  register: connection_test\n\n- name: Gather ansible facts\n  ansible_setup:\n    gather_subset: all\n  become: false\n\n- name: Install bootstrap packages\n  package:\n    name: "{{ bootstrap_facts_packages }}"\n    state: present\n    become_flags: "{{ bootstrap_become_flags | default(\'\')}}" \n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:21:43.737202964Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9213400189, 'load_duration': 85408001, 'prompt_eval_count': 439, 'prompt_eval_duration': 93054993, 'eval_count': 601, 'eval_duration': 9034354718, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7159c751-3859-4375-920f-b30126ae5e69-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 439, 'output_tokens': 601, 'total_tokens': 1040}
