content='<think>\nOkay, so I need to fix the Ansible Playbook that didn\'t pass ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors and figure out what\'s wrong.\n\nFirst, the errors mention that the \'members\' parameter for the group module isn\'t supported. Oh right, I remember that the group module doesn\'t take \'members\' anymore. Instead, you should use \'group\' module with \'state\' and \'users\' or manage it through other means. Wait, actually, the group module can manage members by including them in the group, but perhaps a better approach is to use the user module to add the user to the group.\n\nLooking at the first task, it\'s using the group module with members. That\'s causing the error. So I should replace that with the user module, which allows me to add a user to a group. So for each user in docker_users, I can loop and add them to the docker group.\n\nNext, the second task uses the shell module to restart SSH. Ansible-lint is complaining about using \'service\' as a command instead of the module. So I should replace that with the service module. Also, the shell module is being used, but it\'s better to use the appropriate module for the task.\n\nAnother issue is the use of \'ansible.builtin.group\' instead of \'ansible.legacy.group\'. Wait, no, the error says to use FQCN, so I should use \'ansible.builtin.user\' because that\'s the correct FQCN for managing users and groups.\n\nSo, for Task 1, I\'ll loop over docker_users and for each user, add them to the docker group using the user module. That way, I avoid the \'members\' parameter issue and use the correct module.\n\nFor Task 2, I\'ll replace the shell command with the service module to restart SSH. This addresses the command-instead-of-module error.\n\nI also need to make sure that the modules are using their FQCNs. So group becomes ansible.builtin.user and shell becomes ansible.builtin.service.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll structure the tasks accordingly, ensuring that the loop is correctly applied to add each user to the group and that the service is restarted properly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Add Docker users to the docker group\n  become: true\n  ansible.builtin.user:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    groups: docker\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ docker_users }}"\n\n- name: Reset SSH connection after user changes\n  become: true\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: ssh\n    state: restarted\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:33:03.905918785Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11439962431, 'load_duration': 90124732, 'prompt_eval_count': 2065, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1084286692, 'eval_count': 539, 'eval_duration': 10263657245, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a4900242-f01c-470a-85ad-a08d97f4e2f2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2065, 'output_tokens': 539, 'total_tokens': 2604}
