pplied, the system reboots if necessary.\n\nTask 4.2 loops over the selinux_booleans variable. For each boolean, I\'ll set the state, ensure it\'s persistent, and use the item\'s name as the label. This will apply the necessary SELinux boolean configurations.\n\nI also need to make sure that all tasks are named exactly as specified and in the correct order. No additional tasks should be added or omitted.\n\nNow, putting it all together in YAML format, I\'ll structure each task under the tasks list. Each task will have the correct module, arguments, and any conditionals or loops as needed.\n\nI should avoid any comments or explanations since the user specified only the YAML playbook without any extra text. Also, ensure that the YAML is properly indented and formatted.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to make sure it adheres to all the given instructions and that each task is correctly implemented. This should meet the user\'s requirements and be valid within an Ansible Role\'s tasks directory.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_file:\n    state: present\n    file: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  only_once: true\n\n- name: Install required packages\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ selinux_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n  notify: Gather facts\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  block:\n    - name: Manage SELinux settings\n      selinux:\n        state: "{{ selinux_state }}"\n        policy: "{{ selinux_policy }}"\n      notify: Reboot\n\n    - name: Manage SELinux booleans\n      loop: "{{ selinux_booleans | default([]) }}"\n      selinux_bool:\n        name: "{{ item.name }}"\n        state: "{{ item.state }}"\n        persistent: yes\n        label: "{{ item.label }}"\n  when:\n    - selinux_status is defined\n    - connection is not in [ \'container\', \'docker\', \'community.docker.docker\' ]\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'create