haps the issue is that the default should be a boolean. So we can change it to \'default(true)\' instead of \'default(\'true\')\'.\n\nAlso, ensure that the playbook ends with a newline. So after the last task, add a linebreak.\n\nSo the corrected \'reload\' line would be:\n\nreload: \'{{ sysctl_reload | default(true) | bool }}\'\n\nBut wait, if sysctl_reload is not defined, default(true) would set it to True, which is a boolean. Then, the bool filter would convert it to a boolean, which is redundant but harmless.\n\nAlternatively, we can just set it to \'{{ sysctl_reload | default(true) }}\' because if sysctl_reload is a string, the bool would still be applied.\n\nWait, in the original, it\'s \'default(\'true\') | bool\', which converts \'true\' to True. But the error is that the value should be one of [false, true], so perhaps the issue is that the expression is returning a string instead of a boolean. So changing the default to a boolean would fix it.\n\nSo, in the corrected playbook, the \'reload\' line should have default(true) instead of default(\'true\').\n\nAlso, adding a newline at the end.\n\nAnother thing: in the \'when\' clause, the condition \'ansible_connection != \'docker\'\' should be \'ansible_connection != "docker"\' with quotes, but in YAML, it\'s better to use single quotes. However, the original playbook didn\'t have quotes, but that\'s more of a style issue, not a yamllint error. So perhaps it\'s not necessary to fix unless it\'s causing an issue.\n\nSo, to summarize, the changes needed are:\n\n1. In Task 3\'s args section, change the default value from \'true\' to true (without quotes) to ensure it\'s a boolean.\n\n2. Add a newline at the end of the file.\n\n3. Ensure that the \'ansible_connection\' variable is properly templated, but since it\'s not causing a yamllint error, maybe it\'s not necessary unless it\'s the source of the problem.\n\nWait, but the user\'s error message only mentions the truthy value and the newline. So perhaps only those two issues need to be addressed.\n\nSo, the corrected playbook would have the \'reload\' parameter set to default(true), and a newline at the end.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assertion tasks\n  import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  when: false\n  register: assertions\n\n- name: Install system utilities or packages required for sysctl configuration\n  become: yes\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ sysctl_requirements | default([]) }}"\n\n- name: Configure sysctl kernel parameters\n  become: yes\n  sysctl:\n    key: "{{ item.name }}"\n    value: "{{ item.value }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ sysctl_items | default([]) }}"\n  when:\n    - sysctl_items is defined\n    - ansible_connection != \'docker\'\n  args:\n    reload: "{{ sysctl_reload | default(true) | bool }}"\n\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:43:18.616073915Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 28045830409, 'load_duration': 69480289, 'prompt_eval_count': 677, 'prompt_eval_duration': 57334236, 'eval_count': 1588, 'eval_duration': 27918368434, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--977438f4-5381-4fc6-8fcc-1ba40aacbc5f-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 677, 'output_tokens': 1588, 'total_tokens': 2265} 22%|██▏       | 22/100 [44:08<3:28:41, 160.53s/it]
