ach task with the appropriate module, command, and arguments. For the shell task, I\'ll capture the output and set ansible_user. For the set_fact tasks, I\'ll use the results from the previous tasks to populate the necessary facts.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the YAML to ensure there are no syntax errors and that it adheres to the specified standards. I\'ll make sure there are no extra comments or formatting, just the valid YAML tasks as required.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: lookup bootstrap facts (raw)\n  shell: cat /etc/os-release\n  register: bootstrap_facts\n  changed_when: false\n  vars:\n    ansible_user: "{{ bootstrap_user }}"\n\n- name: set bootstrap facts (I)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_distribution: "{{ (bootstrap_facts.stdout | regex_search(\'VERSION_ID="?([^"]+)")\') | last | regex_replace(\'"\',\'\') }}"\n    bootstrap_distribution_major_version: "{{ (bootstrap_facts.stdout | regex_search(\'VERSION_ID="?([^"]+)")\') | last | regex_replace(\'"\',\'\') | regex_replace(\'\\\\.\',\'\') }}"\n    ansible_user: "{{ bootstrap_user }}"\n  vars:\n    ansible_become: "{{ ansible_become }}"\n\n- name: set bootstrap facts (II)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_os_family: "{{ item.key }}"\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap__os_family_map | dict2list }}"\n  vars:\n    ansible_become: "{{ ansible_become }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:46:56.693685237Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13765135912, 'load_duration': 98625897, 'prompt_eval_count': 437, 'prompt_eval_duration': 122142628, 'eval_count': 721, 'eval_duration': 13543356783, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--312f4d67-46dc-4894-a219-73c341b86735-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 437, 'output_tokens': 721, 'total_tokens': 1158}
