 is set to false.\n\nTask 6: Configure yum by using dnf on CentOS/RHEL 6 and yum otherwise. I\'ll use the yum module with \'name: yum-utils\' to install it. Also, I need a condition to check if the OS is RHEL 6 or CentOS 6, in which case I use dnf. Otherwise, use yum. I\'ll use \'ansible_facts\' to check the distribution version.\n\nTask 7: Update with zypper. Use zypper with \'state: latest\' and \'changed_when\' to false.\n\nI need to structure each task correctly, making sure to use the correct modules and parameters. Also, for Task 6, I should use \'when\' condition to execute the yum task only if the OS is not RHEL/CentOS 6.\n\nI\'ll also make sure that each task is in the correct order, as specified, and that I don\'t add or omit any tasks. All tasks must be present and in the given order.\n\nFinally, I\'ll write the YAML, ensuring proper indentation and that each task is correctly formatted. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations outside the YAML structure, as per the user\'s request.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  block:\n    - name: assert.yml imported\n      assert:\n        that: "\'test\' in \'test\'"\n        success_msg: "Imported assert.yml successfully"\n\n- name: Configure apk\n  apk:\n    update_cache: yes\n    upgrade: all\n    state: present\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Configure apt\n  apt:\n    state: present\n    upgrade: yes\n    name:\n      - package1\n      - package2\n    noninteractive: yes\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Update all software (dnf)\n  dnf:\n    name: "*"\n    state: latest\n    exclude:\n      - packageA\n      - packageB\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Update all software (pacman)\n  pacman:\n    state: latest\n    upgrade: all\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Configure yum\n  yum:\n    name: yum-utils\n    state: present\n  when:ansible_distribution in [\'CentOS\', \'RedHat\'] and ansible_distribution_major_version == \'6\'\n\n- n