content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. Let me go through each task step by step to ensure I cover everything correctly.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the first line. I\'ll make sure that\'s included.\n\nFor Task 1, I need to check if the Helm binary exists. The user specified using the stat module and registering the result to helm_check. So, I\'ll use stat with path=/usr/local/bin/helm and register it as helm_check.\n\nNext, Task 2 is about checking the Helm version. The task says to execute helm version and register the output to helm_existing_version. I\'ll use the command module here, setting the command to helm version and register the output as required.\n\nMoving on to Task 3, the goal is to download the specified Helm version using the unarchive module. The download should only happen if Helm isn\'t installed or the version doesn\'t match. I\'ll use the unarchive module, specifying the remote_src and the Helm URL. I need to include the version variable here, so I\'ll make sure to include it in the playbook.\n\nTask 4 involves copying the Helm binary to the correct location with appropriate permissions. I\'ll use the copy module, set the remote_src to the downloaded Helm file, and the destination as /usr/local/bin/helm. I\'ll also set the file mode to 0755 and use become to escalate privileges if needed.\n\nI need to ensure all tasks are in the correct order and use the exact names provided. Also, I must avoid adding any hosts, vars, or playbook-level headers since this is meant for an Ansible Role under tasks/main.yml.\n\nI should also check that the YAML is valid, adhering to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. Each task should be properly indented and structured without any extra comments or explanations.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure to include the \'---\' at the beginning and structure each task correctly under it, ensuring the playbook can be directly included in the role without any issues.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if Helm binary exists\n  stat:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/helm\n  register: helm_check\n\n- name: Check Helm version\n  command: helm version\n  register: helm_existing_version\n\n- name: Download helm\n  unarchive:\n    remote_src: yes\n    url: https://get.helm.sh/helm-{{ helm_version }}-linux-amd64.tar.gz\n    dest: /tmp\n  register: helm_download\n  when:\n    - helm_check.stat is not defined or\n    - helm_existing_version.stdout is not defined or\n    - helm_existing_version.stdout | version_compare(\'version\') != 0\n\n- name: Copy helm binary into place\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: "{{ helm_download.src }}/linux-amd64/helm"\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/helm\n    mode: 0755\n  become: yes\n  when: helm_download is not skipped\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T18:56:41.757582564Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9259689406, 'load_duration': 77315821, 'prompt_eval_count': 409, 'prompt_eval_duration': 95906122, 'eval_count': 642, 'eval_duration': 9085095369, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--b060c10c-3f81-4c00-bfee-ddff70847461-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 409, 'output_tokens': 642, 'total_tokens': 1051}
