\'ll structure the playbook with two tasks. The first task handles enabling the modules, checking the OS family, and using apt or zypper accordingly. Then, it enables the modules and restarts Apache. The second task uses the template to configure the locations and then restarts Apache again to ensure all changes are applied.\n\nI should also make sure that the YAML syntax is correct, with proper indentation and line breaks. No extra comments or explanations, just the tasks as specified. Let me double-check the module names and parameters to ensure they match what\'s required. Everything seems in order, so I\'ll proceed to write the playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: locations | Enable modules\n  become: yes\n  apt:\n    name:\n      - state=installed\n      - name=apache2\n      - name=apache2-utils\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n  register: apt_result\n\n  # For Suse-based systems\n  apt:\n    name:\n      - state=installed\n      - name=apache2\n      - name=apache2-utils\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Suse"\n\n  shell: a2enmod proxy proxy_http\n  args:\n    chdir: /etc/apache2/mods-enabled\n\n  notify: restart apache\n\n- name: locations | Configure locations\n  template:\n    src: httpd_locations.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/apache2/sites-available/httpd_locations.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ httpd_locations | default([]) }}"\n\n  notify: restart apache\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T19:28:00.728413236Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13238448417, 'load_duration': 87078960, 'prompt_eval_count': 309, 'prompt_eval_duration': 75619736, 'eval_count': 768, 'eval_duration': 13075097591, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--256cc06e-168f-4d86-a447-2b07e8f0e2bb-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 309, 'output_tokens': 768, 'total_tokens': 1077}
