content='<think>\nOkay, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the error messages and figure out what\'s wrong.\n\nFirst, I see that there are issues with using the correct module names. The error messages mention that we should use FQCN (Fully Qualified Common Names) for modules. So, instead of \'file\', \'template\', and \'apt\', we should use \'ansible.builtin.file\', \'ansible.builtin.template\', and \'ansible.builtin.apt\'.\n\nNext, there are problems with octal values. Ansible-lint doesn\'t like implicit octal values like 0755 or 0644. To fix this, I should convert these to decimal or use quotes to make them strings. For example, 0755 becomes 511 in decimal, or we can just keep them as strings like \'0755\'.\n\nLooking at the apt module, there are unsupported parameters like \'creates\', \'enable\', and \'mode\'. The apt module doesn\'t support these. I need to remove them. Also, the \'state\' parameter should be \'present\' for enabling the package, but actually, for a2ensite, maybe we should use a different approach or use the correct module.\n\nWait, in the third task, the module is \'apt\' which is not the right module for enabling virtual hosts. The \'a2ensite\' command is part of the apache2-utils module. So, I should replace the apt module with the apt module for package management and perhaps use the command module to run a2ensite. But wait, the user\'s instruction was to correct the playbook without altering the functional intent. So, perhaps the apt module was a mistake, and it should be using the correct module for enabling the site.\n\nWait, looking back, the original task says to use a2ensite, which is a shell command. So maybe the module should be \'shell\' or \'command\' instead of \'apt\'. But in the faulty playbook, the module is \'apt\', which is incorrect. So I need to change that.\n\nBut let me check the error messages again. The apt module in the playbook is being used with parameters that it doesn\'t support. So, the task is using the wrong module. The correct module for running a2ensite would be command or shell.\n\nSo, for task 3, I should replace the apt module with the command module, specifying the a2ensite command. Also, I need to ensure that this task only runs on Debian systems, so the when condition should check ansible_os_family == "Debian".\n\nLet me outline the steps:\n\n1. For each task, replace the module with its FQCN. So \'file\' becomes \'ansible.builtin.file\', \'template\' becomes \'ansible.builtin.template\', and \'apt\' becomes \'ansible.builtin.apt\'.\n\n2. Convert octal values to either decimal or quoted strings. So 0755 becomes 511, but actually, in YAML, using quotes allows us to keep the octal notation. So \'0755\' as a string.\n\n3. Remove unsupported parameters from the apt module. Wait, but in the faulty playbook, the third task uses apt, which is incorrect. So I need to change that task to use the correct module.\n\nWait, the third task is supposed to enable virtual hosts using a2ensite, which is a shell command. Therefore, the module should be command, not apt. So, I\'ll change the module to command and set the command as \'a2ensite {{ item.name }}.conf\'.\n\nAlso, the creates attribute in the faulty playbook points to the config file, which is correct, but since we\'re switching to command, the creates should point to the symlink location, perhaps /etc/apache2/sites-enabled/... or similar. Alternatively, perhaps the creates attribute isn\'t needed anymore if the command creates the symlink.\n\nWait, the a2ensite command creates a symlink in /etc/apache2/sites-enabled. So the creates attribute should point to that path. So, I\'ll set creates: "/etc/apache2/sites-enabled/{{ item.name }}.conf".\n\nAdditionally, the notify part should still be there to restart httpd after the changes.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll adjust each task as follows:\n\n- Task 1: Use ansible.builtin.file, set mode to \'0755\' as a string, and adjust the loop condition.\n\n- Task 2: Use ansible.builtin.template, mode \'0644\' as a string.\n\n- Task 3: Replace apt with command, set the command to a2ensite, and adjust the creates attribute.\n\nI\'ll also make sure that all other parameters are correctly set and that the YAML syntax is correct.\n\nNow, I\'ll rewrite the playbook with these fixes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create docroot directories for each virtual host\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ item.documentroot }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts if httpd_vhosts | default | list }}"\n  when:\n    - httpd_vhosts is defined\n    - item.documentroot is defined\n    - create_docroot | default(true) | bool\n  loop_control:\n    loop_var: item\n\n- name: Configure virtual host settings\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: vhost_conf_template\n    dest: "{{ httpd_vhosts_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n    mode: \'0644\'\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts if httpd_vhosts | default | list }}"\n  when: httpd_vhosts is defined\n  loop_control:\n    loop_var: item\n\n- name: Enable virtual hosts on Debian systems\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: a2ensite "{{ item.name }}.conf"\n    creates: "{{ httpd_vhosts_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n  notify:\n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n  loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts if httpd_vhosts | default | list }}"\n  loop_control:\n    loop_var: item\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T19:33:15.976363194Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 24914279557, 'load_duration': 85929245, 'prompt_eval_count': 2523, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1310953128, 'eval_count': 1300, 'eval_duration': 23516070494, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--eb0ea469-3654-4cfd-8814-435c43a462cf-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2523, 'output_tokens': 1300, 'total_tokens': 3823}
