ourth task is about configuring httpd, which seems fine. \n\nThe fifth task activates httpd modules on Debian, using apt with state present. That looks okay. \n\nThe sixth to tenth tasks import other yml files, which seems correct. \n\nThe eleventh task is to flush handlers, which is correct. \n\nThe twelfth task removes the default HTML file, which is fine. \n\nThe thirteenth task starts and enables httpd, which looks correct.\n\nNow, the second yamllint error is about the lack of a trailing newline. So I need to ensure that the playbook ends with a newline. In the faulty playbook, the last line is the service task without a trailing newline, causing the error. So adding a newline at the end will fix that.\n\nAdditionally, I should check for any other potential issues, but the user only provided two error messages, so focusing on those.\n\nSo, to summarize, the fixes are:\n\n1. In the \'Configure selinux\' task, change the \'state\' parameter to use yesno filter to convert boolean to \'enforcing\' or \'disabled\'.\n2. Ensure the playbook ends with a trailing newline.\n\nI\'ll make these changes in the corrected playbook.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Install apache httpd\n  become: true\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  become_flags: sudo\n  when: ansible_os_family == \'Debian\'\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  become: true\n  selinux:\n    boolean: httpd_selinux_booleans\n    state: "{{ selinux_enabled | yesno(\'enforcing\',\'disabled\') }}"\n  when: ansible_selinux_enabled\n\n- name: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: httpd.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_file }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify:\n    - httpd_config_test\n    - httpd_restart\n\n- name: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  become: true\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  with_items: "{{ httpd_modules }}"\n  when: ansible_os_family == \'Debian\'\n\n- name: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n\n- name: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n\n- name: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n\n- name: Configure ports\n  become: true\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_ports }}"\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_os_family in [\'Debian\', \'Suse\']\n  notify:\n    - httpd_config_test\n    - httpd_restart\n\n- name: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Removing default html\n  file:\n    path: "{{ apache_default_html }}"\n    state: absent\n  when: httpd_remove_example\n\n- name: Start and enable httpd\n  become: true\n  service:\n    name: apache2\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  become_flags: sudo\n\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T20:01:18.525422052Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 28098382313, 'load_duration': 94225401, 'prompt_eval_count': 1211, 'prompt_eval_duration': 62551188, 'eval_count': 1583, 'eval_duration': 27940475620, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--582dc12d-1765-43b5-9999-070519d585eb-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1211, 'output_tokens': 1583, 'total_tokens': 2794} 58%|█████▊    | 58/100 [2:02:08<1:40:10, 143.11s/it]
