content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given instructions. Let me start by understanding the requirements.\n\nFirst, the playbook must begin with \'---\' on the very first line. That\'s straightforward.\n\nNext, it should be a valid YAML file, adhering to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. So I need to make sure the syntax is correct, indentation is proper, and all key-value pairs are correctly formatted.\n\nThe playbook should be structured to be included directly in an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory, specifically tasks/main.yml. That means I shouldn\'t include any playbook-level headers like hosts: or vars: since those are typically defined elsewhere in the role structure.\n\nNow, looking at the tasks:\n\nTask 1: Import assert.yml. I need to use the import_tasks module. The arguments should be file=assert.yml and run_once=true. Also, I should delegate this task to localhost because it\'s likely a local task.\n\nTask 2: Manage automatic service management. This task involves checking if the package manager is apt and then taking action based on the apt_autostart_state variable. \n\nInside the conditional block for apt, if apt_autostart_state is "disabled", I need to copy a file to /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d with the content "exit 101" and mode 755. If it\'s "enabled", I should remove that file.\n\nI should use the apt module with the state parameter set to stopped when autostart is disabled. Also, I\'ll use the copy module for creating the policy-rc.d file and file module for removing it.\n\nI need to make sure that the tasks are in the correct order and that all modules are used properly. Also, I should check that the variables are correctly referenced, like apt_autostart_state.\n\nI\'ll structure the tasks as a list under the main.yml file. The first task is the import_tasks, and the second task is the apt with a conditional block.\n\nI also need to ensure that the YAML doesn\'t have any trailing spaces or incorrect indentation. Each task should be a separate entry in the list, with proper keys like name, action, etc.\n\nLet me draft the YAML now, making sure each task is correctly formatted and adheres to the requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- import_tasks: assert.yml\n  run_once: true\n  delegate_to: localhost\n\n- name: Manage automatic service management for apt\n  apt:\n    state: stopped\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'apt\'\n  register: apt_autostart_state\n\n- name: Disable apt autostart\n  copy:\n    content: \'exit 101\\n\'\n    dest: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n    mode: 755\n  when: apt_autostart_state == "disabled"\n\n- name: Enable apt autostart\n  file:\n    state: absent\n    path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n  when: apt_autostart_state == "enabled"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-09T20:03:54.015641868Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11082056951, 'load_duration': 81197990, 'prompt_eval_count': 378, 'prompt_eval_duration': 92543128, 'eval_count': 632, 'eval_duration': 10907663539, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--d1d490a9-6dfe-421c-bc81-a877910e1ea3-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 378, 'output_tokens': 632, 'total_tokens': 1010}
