his.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I'll start with the '---' line, then define each task in the specified order, using 'when' conditions where necessary. For tasks that apply to both OS families, I'll omit the 'when' condition.\n\nI should also ensure that the playbook doesn't include any explanations or comments beyond what's necessary for the YAML structure. Each task should be a valid Ansible task entry without any extra fluff.\n\nFinally, I'll double-check that all tasks are included exactly as described and that the playbook is valid for inclusion in an Ansible Role under the tasks/main.yml file.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Update apt cache\n  apt:\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: Update dnf cache\n  dnf:\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: Install packages\n  apt:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'\n\n- name: Install packages\n  dnf:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'\n\n- name: Create directory for keepalived\n  file:\n    path: /etc/keepalived\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for Debian OS family\n  template:\n    src: k8s_api_health.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_health.sh\n    mode: 0755\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'\n  notify: restart_keepalived\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for RedHat OS family\n  template:\n    src: k8s_api_health.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/k8s_api_health.sh\n    mode: 0755\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'\n  notify: restart_keepalived\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for Debian OS family\n  template:\n    src: rke2_server_health.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2_server_health.sh\n    mode: 0755\n  when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'\n  notify: restart_keepalived\n\n- name: Create RKE2 Server health check script for RedHat OS family\n  template:\n    src: rke2_server_health.sh.j2\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/rke2